/-!
# The ideal of a subbundle, and its regularity over a closed subscheme of the base

Let `0 ⟶ 𝒩' ⟶ 𝒩 ⟶ ℰ ⟶ 0` be a short exact sequence of finite locally free `𝒪_X`-modules, of
ranks `r'`, `r`, `e`, and `i : N' ⟶ N` the closed embedding of their vector bundles. Over an
affine open `V ⊆ X` the ring of `N` is `Γ(N, p⁻¹ V) = Sym_{Γ(X, V)}(Γ(𝒩^∨, V))`, the ideal of
`N'` is generated by the image of `Γ(ℰ^∨, V)` in degree one, and when `ℰ^∨` and `(𝒩')^∨` are free
on `V` the ring is a polynomial ring `Γ(X, V)[x_1, …, x_e, y_1, …, y_{r'}]` in which these
generators are the variables `x_j`. Consequently, for every closed subscheme `Y ⊆ X`, the ideal
of `N'` in the local rings of the inverse image `p⁻¹ Y` is generated by a regular sequence of
length `e`: this is item (3) of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FAA], that `(p')⁻¹ Y ⟶ p⁻¹ Y` is a
regular immersion.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.bundleChartEquiv` — `Γ(𝐕(ℱ), p⁻¹ V) ≅ Sym_{Γ(X, V)}(Γ(ℱ, V))` over an affine
  open `V`.
* `Stacks.Chow.subbundleCosectionFn` — the function on `p⁻¹ V` attached to a section of `ℰ^∨`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.ker_subbundleEmbedding_ideal_eq_span` — the ideal of `N'` over `V` is generated by
  the functions attached to a basis of `Γ(ℰ^∨, V)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_polyEquiv` — the polynomial chart adapted to `N'`.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_isRegular_stalk_comap_subbundle` — the regularity statement above.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FAA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FAA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01LX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01LX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00LL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00LL)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

